  "outlookText": "000\nACPN50 PHFO 060508\nTWOCP \n\nTropical Weather Outlook\nNWS Central Pacific Hurricane Center Honolulu HI\nIssued by NWS National Hurricane Center Miami FL\n800 PM HST Thu Nov 05 2026\n\nFor the central North Pacific...between 140W and 180W:\n\nEastern Central Pacific (CP95):\nShowers and thunderstorms associated with an area of low pressure\nlocated several hundred miles to the southeast of the Big Island of\nHawaii continue to show signs of organization.  Environmental\nconditions are conducive for additional development, and a tropical\ndepression is expected to develop on Friday.  The system is\nforecast to move west-northwestward to westward at 10 to 15 mph,\npassing well south of the Hawaiian Islands.\n* Formation chance through 48 hours...high...90 percent.\n* Formation chance through 7 days...high...90 percent.\n\n$$\nForecaster Blake\nNNNN",
